The depletion chance of a tree falling when cut is rolled as 1/X, where X is the greater value between: 2x number of players at the start of the raid, OR 3. In the ice demon room, multiply that value by 5. For example, in a raid that had 5 players, 2x number of players at the start of the raid is 2x5, i.e. 10. That's at least 3. So normally the chance of depletion is 1/10, but in the ice demon room it'd be 1/50. In a solo raid, 2x number of players at the start of the raid is 2x1, i.e. 2. We'd use 3 because that's greater. So normally the chance of depletion is 1/3, but in the ice demon room it'd be 1/15.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://x.com/JagexAsh/status/1277201627997515778|date=28 June 2020|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/27964243|archivedate=28 July 2026|quote=The depletion chance normally is 1/X where X is: 3, or Party size x 2 whichever is higher. In the Ice Demon room, X is multiplied by 5 to make depletion rarer.}}

There are four [[brazier (Chambers of Xeric)|braziers]] surrounding the demon. [[Kindling (Chambers of Xeric)|Kindling]] can be used to light these braziers to slowly dispel the ice storm. A player's [[Firemaking]] level affects their chance of successfully lighting a brazier, using the standard Firemaking skill roll with an 8% success chance at level 1, scaling to 78% at level 99.{{CiteDiscord|author=Mod Ash|url=https://discord.com/channels/324132423636090880/434286997360738305/1527317975521300510|date=16 July 2026|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/27964244#chat-messages-434286997360738305-1527317975521300510|archivedate=28 July 2026|quote=Yes - it's a normal skill-roll, using 8% success at level 1 and scaling up linearly to 78% at level 99.}}

Additionally, an [[icefiend]] occupies each brazier (one icefiend for each player in the team, capping at four icefiends). They do not move, but if the brazier next to them is lit, they will attempt to remove a charge from it every 3 to 4 ticks, with a 1/6 chance of succeeding.{{CiteDiscord|author=Mod Ash|url=https://discord.com/channels/324132423636090880/434286997360738305/1526211486844715088|date=13 July 2026|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/27964245#chat-messages-434286997360738305-1526211486844715088|archivedate=28 July 2026|quote=Correct. Regardless of whether the fiend decided to wait 3 ticks or 4 ticks before it next executed its action, the action contains a 1/6 deduction chance. It's like having a weapon with an attack rate that's either 3 or 4, randomly, and that has a 1/6 chance of succeeding when it attacks.}}

Once the ice storm is dispelled, the icefiends will disappear and the demon will emerge from the storm to engage the team. It has two attacks; a snow boulder and Ice Burst. The demon will take overhead prayers into account when fighting them; if the target is using [[Protect from Missiles]], it will only use the snow boulder attack. If [[Protect from Magic]] is used instead, it will only use Ice Burst. Both attacks are AoE with a 3x3 radius, so one can avoid attacks completely by moving a few spaces away from their spot. It is recommended to use Protect from Missiles, as the ice burst projectile is nearly impossible to spot and is much faster than the boulder.

The demon has low health compared to other monster puzzles, but compensates for this with high Defence and a damage reduction effect.

All damage dealt to the demon is reduced by 67%, except for [[fire spells]] (which deal 250% damage) and [[demonbane weapons]] (in which all demonbane modifiers are increased by 15%). Magic attacks are effective due to the demon's magic defence being calculated from its Defence level rather than Magic, unlike most monsters.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1101198072300875778|date=28 February 2019|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/103722|archivedate=28 May 2020|quote=Most NPCs calculate magical defence from the Magic stat. Some, now including this one, calculate it from the Defence stat - and for this demon, the Defence stat is much lower. (Monster Examine?) So magic will be more accurate there. Fire spells have always done + damage to it.}}

The ice demon regenerates its stats at the standard rate of 1 per 100 ticks.{{CiteDiscord|author=Mod Ash|url=https://discord.com/channels/324132423636090880/434286997360738305/1524701424460628080|date=9 July 2026|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/27964246#chat-messages-434286997360738305-1524701424460628080|archivedate=28 July 2026|quote=Stone guardians - 8 Muttadiles - 15 Vasa Nistirio - 10 Vasa's crystal - 9 Tekton - 15 LizardShamans - 20 Skeletal mystics - 25 Jewelled Crabs - 1 Vespula - 10 Vespula's portal - 45 Vespula's grubs - 10000 (i.e. never) Vespine soldier (flying) - 16 Vespine soldier (walking) - 10000 Otherwise default should be 100, as for outside CoX.|ctxquote=Hi@JagexAsh would you per chance be able to say the regen time (in ticks) for mobs in chambers?}}

It is recommended to use [[dragon warhammer]] or [[Bandos godsword]] special attacks to lower the demon's defences, unless using them in the following room is more advantageous (for example, against [[Tekton]]). The [[twisted bow]] hits well against the ice demon due to its high Magic level, but fire spells are still superior if the player can afford to bring it, but both are outclassed by [[Emberlight]] if the player is not using [[Fire Surge]] with a [[Harmonised Nightmare staff]].

